chapter.p:
Yes, you will be ashamed of your sacred oaks which have given you delight;
you will blush for your gardens
which you have chosen.

He gives a signal to nations afar,
he whistles to them from the ends of the earth;
speedily and swiftly they come.

None of them is weary, none stumbles none slumbers or sleeps;
not a waist belt is loosened,
not a sandal-thong broken.

therefore the Lord will bring against them the waters of the River, deep and mighty – the king of Assyria with all his pomp.
It will rise over all its channels
and overflow all its banks;

Know it, O you nations.
Hear, O you distant lands;
gird yourselves for war and be dismayed!

Was it not the same for Calno as for Carchemish,
for Hamath as for Arpad,
and for Samaria as for Damascus?

They have crossed over the pass and now camp at Geba for the night.
Ramah is in terror;
Gibeah of Saul has fled.

Yahweh Sabaoth has sworn:
“As I have planned, so will it be!
As I have decided, so will I do;

Like a lyre, therefore,
my soul moans for Moab;
my heart pines for Kir-areseth.

The princes of Zoan have become fools;
the princes of Memphis have been deceived;
Egypt is led astray by the chiefs of her tribes.

If he sees riders:
horsemen in pairs,
men mounted on camels,
men mounted on donkeys;
let him observe diligently,
let him listen attentively.”

These people have fled from the sword,
from the whetted swords,
from the bent bows,
from the fury of battle.

Elam bears the quiver
with charioteers and horsemen;
Kir uncovers the shield.

Chariots are all over your choicest valleys;
horsemen are stationed at the gates.
Judah is stripped of her defenses.

He has said, “Rejoice no longer, ravished virgin daughter of Sidon.
Arise, pass over to Cyprus;
even there you will find no rest.”

There will be a highway which will be called The Way of Holiness;
no one unclean will pass over it
nor any wicked fool stray there.

My anguish has turned to peace; you have retrieved my life
from the pit of corruption;
you have cast all my sins behind you.

For the dead cannot give you thanks, death cannot give you praise;
those who go down to the pit
cannot hope for your kindness.

Every valley will be raised up;
every mountain and hill will be laid low.
The stumbling blocks shall become level and the rugged places smooth.

The glory of Yahweh will be revealed,
and all mortals together will see it;
for the mouth of Yahweh has spoken.”

Here comes your God with might;
his strong arm rules for him;
his reward is with him,
and here before him is his booty.

I will plant in the wilderness the cedar,
the acacia, the myrtle and the olive;
I will plant in the wasteland fir, cypress and pine –

All of them are nothing,
emptiness are their works;
their images are wind and nothingness.

He will not waver or be broken
until he has established justice on earth;
the islands are waiting for his law.

I, Yahweh, have called you for the sake of justice;
I will hold your hand to make you firm;
I will make you as a covenant to the people,
and as a light to the nations,

I am Yahweh, that is my name,
I will not give my glory to another;
or my praise to graven images.

Sing a new song to Yahweh;
let his praise reach the ends of the earth.
Let the sea and all that it holds, let the coastlands and their inhabitants resound with song and praise of him.

I will lead the blind by ways
which they do not know;
along unseen paths I will guide them. I will turn darkness into light before them and make the rough ground smooth. These are the things that I will do, and I will not forsake them.

When you pass through the waters, I will be with you.
When you pass through the rivers, they will not sweep over you. When you walk through fire, you will not be burned;
neither will the flames consume you.

Let the nations gather together, let the people assemble. Who among them can foretell this or declare to us the things to come?
Let them bring their witnesses to prove them right;
let others hear so that they may say, “It is true.”

Remember this, Jacob,
for you are my servant, O Israel,
I have formed you to be my servant; Israel, do not forget me.

I will go before you to level the slopes,
I will break the gates of brass
and destroy the iron bars;

I am Yahweh, and there is no other;
there is no God besides me.
I armed you when you did not know me,

I form the light and create the dark;
I usher in prosperity and bring calamity.
I, Yahweh, do all this.

recall those things of long ago.
I am God, and there is no other;
I am God, and there is none like me.

Take the millstone and grind meal;
uncover your hair, bare your legs;
strip to the thighs and pass over the rivers.

Destroyed because of our sins, he was crushed for our wickedness.
Through his punishment we are made whole;
by his wounds we are healed.

With perfumed oil, you made yourself look your best for Molech;
you sent envoys far afield –
the children you sent to your pagan god through a sacrificial death.

Although wearied with your misdeeds,
you have never given up;
you have never tired or weakened, but instead found your strength revived.

Yahweh will guide you always and give you relief in desert places. He will strengthen your bones;
he will make you as a watered garden, like a spring of water
whose waters never fail.

For your hands are blood-stained, your fingers blotted with crimes;
your lips have spoken lies,
your tongues have uttered deceit.

No one fights for a right cause;
no one makes a truthful plea.
They all tell lies and rely on vanity;
they conceive mischief and bring forth iniquity.

The sons of those who oppressed you will come bending low;
all who despised you will fall before your feet.
They will call you the City of Yahweh, Zion of the Holy One of Israel.

Instead of bronze I will bring you gold; instead of iron I will bring silver;
instead of wood, bronze;
instead of stones, iron. Peace will be overseers, justice your taskmasters.

to announce the year of Yahweh’s favor
and the day of vengeance of our God;
to give comfort to all who grieve;
